The root cause of the bug is that the SCSI probing process synchronously creates and destroys multiple request queues back-to-back for non-existent Logical Unit Numbers (LUNs). This leads to significant delays during the shutdown of the blk-mq subsystem, as the `percpu_ref` shutdown involves a scheduler RCU grace period, which takes measurable wallclock time. Consequently, this results in stalls that can exceed ten seconds when using the SCSI multi-queue (scsi-mq) implementation.



